  "research_id": "payment-transparency-hidden-constitution",
  "title": "What stablecoins reveal, and what they still hide",
  "question": "What becomes visible—and to whom—as payment moves from cash and checks to cards, wallets and public-chain stablecoins, and which governing institutions remain behind the interface?",
  "bluf": "Public-chain stablecoins let anyone see transfers, but what makes money trustworthy (who backs it, who can redeem, who can freeze it, what happens after fraud or failure) still sits with institutions behind the screen.",
